{"seq":13,"trial_id":"gbrain-installer-hook-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-heldout/sd-06-pod-end-of-day/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T08:35:13.101Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"f6b4460198ed9aef650ad87abdffe6beebc1a6f1df8faa3ec1c2330a8401fe3f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"The weekday schedule is saved, but it is not right yet, and I haven't fixed it.\n\n- **Wrong time:** the job's next run is set for Mon 2026-10-26 at 17:30 UTC. That's 12:30 Chicago, and it would skip today's note (Wed 2026-10-14). Your request was 17:30 Chicago.\n- **Not running:** the Hermes gateway isn't running, so the job won't fire until it's started.\n- **Posted in #strategic-pod:** two replies to June's message (ts 1791986400.000126). The first said the job was scheduled, and the second corrected the time problem.\n\nThe scheduler only takes UTC times, so the fix is a cron entry that tracks Chicago time. Chicago is UTC-5 until DST ends on Nov 1, then UTC-6. A 22:30 UTC entry gives 17:30 Chicago until Nov 1, and it would then fire at 16:30 Chicago. Keeping 17:30 Chicago year-round means changing the entry on Nov 1, or setting it up on a host that runs in Chicago time.\n\nShould I set it to 22:30 UTC on weekdays for now, with a reminder to adjust on Nov 1? And is the gateway being started on your side?"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1791986400.000129"}}
